{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>For there is no divination in Jacob.</b> The reason He brought them out of Egypt and drove out nations for Israel's sake and gave Israel הֵילֵל רְאֵם, is that they are a generation that seeks Him and do not seek divination, as it says: כִּי הַגּוֹיִם הָאֵלֶּה אֶל מְעֹנְנִים וְאֶל קֹסְמִים יִשְׁמָעוּ וְאַתָּה לֹא כֵן (Deuteronomy 18:14)." "<b>At this time.</b> When they wish to know future events." "<b>It will be said to Jacob and Israel, what has El wrought.</b> It will be told to them through prophecy, or by means of some prophet, what the blessed El has decreed — it will not be told to them what the signs of the heavens indicate or what their astrological configurations produce, because they are not subject to those configurations."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:40:58.692687638Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}